diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index b25515c..c201a1b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@ All notable changes to SparkSpend are listed here in reverse chronological order
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added (which car charged - decided by the charger)
+- **The charger's own session data now decides which car charged** (`ChargerPairing`, `ChargerReconciler`). Real data showed the plug-in time-match picking the wrong car on both of the first two sessions recorded with the extra Home Assistant data: the cars' cloud data arrives hours late and the cable sensors are unreliable. What is reliable is the battery level of the car that charged (it rises between `charge_start` and `charge_end`) and the power signature (Enyaq ~10.5 kW; e-Up never above ~7.5 kW and ~27 kWh, learned from your own labelled charges). Rules: one car's SoC rose >= 5 points while the others did not -> that car (`pairingSource = charger` from +10 points, otherwise `uncertain`); power/energy rule out all but one car -> that car; if the evidence contradicts itself, the charge is left for a human. Runs after every Monta sync and when a session ends; a Monta charge is paired to a session by start/stop time (+-20 min) and energy (+-5 %). New rank order: `manual > api > charger > matched > uncertain > legacy > unknown` - a manual correction is never touched.
+
+### Fixed (data)
+- Two legacy charges (10 Feb 2025) had `vehicleId` stored as a BLOB, so per-car queries (`WHERE vehicleId = 2`) skipped 57.8 kWh. Migration `006_fix_blob_vehicle_ids` casts them to INTEGER.
+
 ### Fixed (dashboard trends)
 - **"vs. forrige mdr" showed a false rise on the last days of a month when the previous month is shorter.** "Same period last month" is the first N days of last month (N = today's day-of-month), cut at that month's last day. On the 31st vs a 30-day month, or the 29th-31st vs February, that window holds fewer days than the current period, so flat usage looked like a rise of about 3 % (31 vs 30 days) up to about 9 % (31 March vs February). The capped window is now scaled to the same number of days (`DashboardWindow::comparableScale`), for kWh and cost of EV, heat pump, house and Rest, and for the pace the projection uses. Nothing changes on days where the window is not capped (28 of 31 days in most months), and the previous month's full-month figure is untouched.
 
